      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the volume of the inscribed sphere, we need to determine its radius first. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube.\n\nThe edge length of the cube is given as 6 inches. Therefore, the diameter of the inscribed sphere is also 6 inches.\n\nThe radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of the diameter. So,\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( r = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\((3)^3\\):\n\n\\[\n(3)^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nNow substitute this value back into the volume formula:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\times 27 \\pi\n\\]\n\n\\[\nV = 36 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36 \\pi}\n\\]",
